; Title: SPACE pressed, wait for it to be released (128K music only)
;
; Called from #R$A336 when SPACE is pressed on the title screen. On the 48K the first byte is a RET, so SPACE does
; nothing. On the 128K the start-up code #R$605F turns the RET into CALL $85EE (the two bytes after it are that
; address), which calls into the music bank at $CA8A; the routine then waits for the key to be released and calls
; #R$85F3 (music bank routine at $C09D). What the two music calls do is Unknown (the 128K code was not run: the
; simulator is 48K).
; .
; Hardware: 128K only: calls into the music player.
;
; O:A 0 (the key code is lost, so the caller's tests for C fail)
@label=WaitSpaceRelease
c$A31E RET           ; 48K: return; 128K: CALL $85EE (patched by #R$605F)
 $A31F DEFB $EE,$85  ; operand of the patched CALL ($85EE)
@label=WaitSpaceRelease_Loop
*$A321 HALT          ; wait for a frame
 $A322 LD A,($A2D2)  ; key code
 $A325 OR A          ;
 $A326 JR NZ,$A321   ;
 $A328 CALL $85F3    ; 128K: music bank routine at $C09D
 $A32B XOR A         ;
 $A32C RET           ;
